  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements: One is labelled as Assertion A and the other is labelled as Reason R:</p><p>Assertion A: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></math> value of phenol is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math> while that of ethanol is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p><p>Reason R: Ethanol is stronger acid than phenol.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EfrNo",
      "text": "A is true but R is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "5JxAq",
      "text": "A is false but R is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IdRNj",
      "text": "Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SNlFq",
      "text": "Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math> is a measure of  the acidity of a particular molecule. It measures the strength of an acid by how tightly a proton is held by a Bronsted acid. The lower the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math>, the stronger the acid and the greater its ability to donate its protons. describe the acidity of a particular molecule.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>pK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>logK</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></math></p><p>Hence, Assertion is true,</p><p>Phenol is more acidic than ethanol because after losing a proton <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfenced></math>, phenol forms phenoxide ion which is stabilised by resonance whereas ethoxide ion is not.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
